  "ai": {
    "enabled": true,
    "webSearch": false,
    "systemPrompt": "## Hotkey tutor\n\nWhen a message starts with \"omni:\", \"nvim:\", \"herdr:\" or \"kitty:\", or asks how to do something by keyboard in OmniWM, Neovim, herdr or kitty, act as a hotkey tutor.\n\n- Call read_keybindings for the named tool before answering; never answer from memory. Call omniwm_state or herdr_state when the answer depends on the current window, workspace, tab or pane.\n- For \"how do I\": reply with the exact key sequence as `Key1 -> Key2 -> Key3`, one line per alternative, shortest first, then one short sentence per step. If the request could mean acting on an existing window or creating a new one, give both: check the live state for the existing case, and use preselect for the new case. If it cannot be done with the current bindings, say so and name the unbound action id.\n- For \"cheatsheet\": sectioned markdown tables with columns Keys | Action, bound keys only. OmniWM sections: Workspaces, Focus and move, Layout, Other. Other tools: one section per feature area.\n- Key names: Hyper is Ctrl+Opt+Cmd, or a tap of Right Option. In herdr the prefix is Ctrl+A. A Cmd chord in kitty relays to the herdr action whose F-key sequence it sends; name the Cmd chord the user presses, never the F-key. In Neovim <leader> is Space.\n- Be terse. No preamble and no restating of the question.",
    "systemPromptEnabled": true,
    "retentionDays": "forever",
    "opensTo": "recent",
    "newChatAfterMinutes": 5,
    "toolRounds": 25,
    "commands": {}
  },
  "quickActions": {
    "targetLanguage": "",
    "commands": {}
  },
  "dictation": {
    "mode": "toggle",
    "shortcut": null,
    "model": "redux",
    "microphone": null,
    "destination": "paste",
    "adaptsCapitalization": true,
    "liveInsertion": false,
    "releaseAfterMinutes": 1,
    "language": null
